@startuml StatePattern
title State Pattern \- Unit Stance (simplified)

interface UnitStance {
  +update(unit : Unit)
  +onDamage(unit : Unit, amount : float)
}

class AttackStance {
  +update(unit : Unit)
  +onDamage(unit : Unit, amount : float)
}

class BuildStance {
  +update(unit : Unit)
  +onDamage(unit : Unit, amount : float)
}

class Stances {
  +defaultStance() : UnitStance
  +attack : UnitStance
  +build : UnitStance
}

class Unit {
  +stance : UnitStance
  +update()
  +damage(amount : float)
}

class RtsAI {
  +evaluate(unit : Unit)
}

class BaseBuilderAI {
  +evaluate(unit : Unit)
}

UnitStance <|.. AttackStance
UnitStance <|.. BuildStance
Unit --> "1" UnitStance : currentStance
RtsAI ..> Unit : "assigns stance"
BaseBuilderAI ..> Unit : "assigns stance"
Stances ..> UnitStance : "preset instances"

note right of Unit
Unit delegates per\-tick and event handling
to its current UnitStance (update, onDamage).
AI classes change the Unit's stance at runtime.
end note

@enduml
